 @artemaung5274  The trade-off is still there. What a "good deal" is depends on what you want and how long you want the GPU to last you. 

Do you want performance for current generation or performance that is more forward looking? 60s are very much focused on being able to run the current generation of games well and doesn't really leave a lot of horsepower headroom for future releases. 

A good deal for today's games is not necessarily a good deal for those next year, the year after that or 4 years down the road.

